new file mode 100644
index 0000000..581e3e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.tightloop/contract.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Goal: Hijack() succeeds after headers are flushed (size==0) but fails once body bytes are written (size>0); websocket libs (e.g. coder/websocket) flush 101 headers before hijacking.
+Acceptance: go test -run TestResponseWriterHijack ./ passes incl. new "after WriteHeaderNow" case, which fails on current code.
+Must not change: hijack-before-write succeeds, hijack-after-Write returns errHijackAlreadyWritten; go test ./... green.
+Non-goals: CloseNotify/Flush, other writers.
+Budget: <30 lines, 2 files.
